From 95df1960a8a62498dcd726ff7cd0f09cd85498eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Toma=C5=BE=20Vajngerl?= <tomaz.vajngerl@collabora.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 16:24:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix bitmap render - don't set device scale on the mip-map
 surface

We shouldn't set the device scale for the mip-map surface, as it
will cause scaling issues.

Change-Id: Icde1d889d386f3c2e78b0c186cac0864b499e77a
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.collaboraoffice.com/c/core/+/1104
Reviewed-by: Miklos Vajna <vmiklos@collabora.com>
Tested-by: Jenkins CPCI <releng@collaboraoffice.com>
(cherry picked from commit f1163666de0e5ac2b40fb27546c36f6192a4e6d9)
(cherry picked from commit f429c0ed5e6f04c3d783d1311b43830d8bbd2e38)
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.libreoffice.org/c/core/+/205986
Tested-by: Jenkins
Reviewed-by: Xisco Fauli <xiscofauli@libreoffice.org>

Comments are condensed to ElyOffice's one-line rule; the code is unchanged.

diff --git a/drawinglayer/source/processor2d/cairopixelprocessor2d.cxx b/drawinglayer/source/processor2d/cairopixelprocessor2d.cxx
index 4e5e7a3..3b65b1f 100644
--- a/drawinglayer/source/processor2d/cairopixelprocessor2d.cxx
+++ b/drawinglayer/source/processor2d/cairopixelprocessor2d.cxx
@@ -641,8 +641,7 @@ public:
         cairo_paint(cr);
         cairo_destroy(cr);
 
-        // set device_scale on downscaled surfaces, as vcl does
-        cairo_surface_set_device_scale(pSurfaceTarget, fScaleX, fScaleY);
+        // no device_scale here: callers' matrices use raw pixels
 
         // add entry to cached entries
         maDownscaled[key] = pSurfaceTarget;
